@startuml csr_end_to_end
title End-to-End CSR: Create Key, Bind and Choose Eager / Batch / DER Input
scale max 3600*3900
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #46535E
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ParticipantBorderColor #596B78
  ParticipantFontColor #20313D
  ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ActorBorderColor #596B78
  GroupBorderColor #596B78
  NoteBackgroundColor #FFF9DC
  NoteBorderColor #C4A15C
}

actor Application as App
box "Client process" #E8F1FF
  participant "Crypto API\nstack, factory and context proxies" as Client
end box
box "Crypto daemon" #F4F7F9
  participant "Mediator\ncontrol-plane dispatch" as Mediator
  participant "HandlerSelector / ProviderArbiter\nand ContextAssembler" as Contexts
  participant "KeyManagementExecutor\nprovider key-management context" as KeyExecutor
  participant "KeyManagementService\nKeyRegistry / DataManager" as Keys
  participant "CsrProcessingContextFactory\nregistered by CsrManagementModule" as CsrFactory
  participant "ProviderManager\ndedicated kCsrProcessing capability" as Providers
  participant "CsrProcessingContextHandler\nclient-owned context" as Processing
  participant "CsrProcessingExecutor\nbackend-independent RPC contract" as Executor
  participant "ICsrProcessor\nOpenSslCsrProcessor in this example" as Processor
  participant "NativeCsrProcessing\nrequest-local helper" as Native
  participant "OpenSSL provider\nkey factory + CSR handler" as Provider
  participant "wire::Decode\nowned input snapshot" as DerWire
  participant "PopulateRequestFromDer\nstrict Name / Extensions" as DerInput
end box

note over App, Provider
  Successful software-provider path, including actual key creation.
  The application receives a key reference, never private-key bytes.
  Transport setup, error paths and repeated helper calls are summarized.
  Generation shows success: validation errors return immediately without signing or publishing output.
end note

group 1. Connect and create a key-management context
  App -> Client : CreateCryptoStack(config)\nthen CreateCryptoContext()
  Client --> App : connected crypto context factory
  App -> Client : CreateKeyManagementContext(key_config)\nprovider type = kSoftware
  Client -> Mediator : CTX_CREATE(KEY:MANAGEMENT)
  Mediator -> Contexts : select provider and assemble context\nno signing key required at this stage
  Contexts -> Provider : create and initialize key-management handler
  Provider --> Contexts : handler using KeyManagementExecutor
  Contexts --> Mediator : key-management context_id
  Mediator --> Client : context_id
  Client --> App : IKeyManagementContext
end

opt 1a. Standalone helpers explicitly requested (not required by generation)
  App -> Client : crypto_context.CreateCsrProcessingContext(config)
  Client -> Mediator : CTX_CREATE(CSR:PROCESSING, empty algorithm)
  Mediator -> Contexts : select registered context factory
  Contexts -> CsrFactory : Create(validated request)
  CsrFactory -> Providers : GetProviderForCapability(kCsrProcessing)\nsoftware-first; existing initialization rules
  Providers --> CsrFactory : available capable IProvider
  CsrFactory -> Provider : IProvider::GetCsrProcessor()
  Provider --> CsrFactory : fresh abstract processor
  CsrFactory -> Executor : construct with injected processor
  Executor --> CsrFactory : executor
  CsrFactory -> Processing : construct fresh handler with executor
  Processing --> CsrFactory : handler
  CsrFactory --> Contexts : handler
  Contexts -> Processing : InitializeContext after adding ContextDataNode
  Processing --> Contexts : initialization status
  Contexts --> Mediator : processing_context_id
  Mediator --> Client : processing_context_id
  Client --> App : ICsrProcessingContext\ncompatible with ICsrProcessingService helpers
  App -> Client : CsrSubject::FromDn(*processing_context, dn)\nor standalone extension/template helpers
  Client -> Mediator : CSR_PROCESS on processing_context_id\nCSR handler actor 13 / action 4; SHM buffers
  Mediator -> Processing : authenticate context ownership and forward
  Processing -> Executor : Execute(input span, output span)
  Executor -> Executor : validate exactly two spans; wire::Decode\nreject Generate and GenerateFromDer
  Executor -> Processor : Process(owned Document)
  Processor -> Native : reuse existing Process(document)
  Native --> Processor : processed Document / native error
  Processor --> Executor : Document / mapped daemon error
  Executor -> Executor : wire::Encode; capacity check; allocate response\nthen copy output bytes
  Executor --> Processing : SHM document + one uint64 written-byte count
  Processing --> Mediator : processing result
  Mediator --> Client : response
  Client --> App : processed value
  note right of CsrFactory
    Only the factory is registered at daemon startup.
    Contexts are created on demand, not by ICryptoStack.
    The former mediator query/action 11 is retired.
    No CSR provider lookup occurs during registration.
    Missing provider / processor fails CTX_CREATE.
  end note
end

group 2. CREATE the private/public key pair and receive its reference
  App -> Client : GenerateKey(params)\nalgorithm = ECDSA-P256, permissions = kSign
  Client -> Mediator : KEY_GENERATE on key-management context_id
  Mediator -> KeyExecutor : forward operation to context handler
  KeyExecutor -> Provider : IKeyFactory::GenerateKey(request)
  Provider -> Provider : generate EC private/public key pair\nretain material in provider-owned key handler
  Provider --> KeyExecutor : IKeyHandler owning the generated key
  KeyExecutor -> Keys : RegisterKeyMaterial(client, parent context,\nprovider, key handler)
  Keys --> KeyExecutor : client-owned key_node_id
  KeyExecutor --> Mediator : key_node_id + provider_id
  Mediator --> Client : key reference identifiers only
  Client --> App : CryptoResourceGuard key_guard\nCryptoResourceId: kKey, kEphemeral
  note over App, Keys
    key_guard identifies this generated key on this connection.
    GenerateKey(params) does not automatically persist it to a slot.
    Keep the guard valid until the CSR context has bound its own reference.
  end note
end

group 3. BIND the returned key reference to a CSR-generation context
  App -> App : csr_config.SetKey(key_guard)\n.SetAlgorithm("ECDSA-P256-SHA256")\n.SetProviderType(kSoftware)
  App -> Client : CreateCsrGenerationContext(csr_config)
  Client -> Mediator : CTX_CREATE(CSR_GENERATION, signature algorithm, ...)\nkey_node_id = key_guard's resource id
  Mediator -> Contexts : select and assemble keyed CSR context
  Contexts -> Keys : ResolveTargetProvider(client, preference, key_node_id)
  Keys --> Contexts : provider compatible with key affinity
  Contexts -> Provider : create CSR handler for signature algorithm
  Provider -> Provider : construct own keyless processor and executor\nno independent processing-provider selection
  Provider --> Contexts : uninitialized CSR handler
  Contexts -> Keys : BindAndAuthorize(client, csr_context_id,\nkey_node_id, provider, kSign, algorithm)
  Keys -> Keys : check ownership, sign permission and compatibility\ncreate context-owned reference to the same key
  Keys --> Contexts : authorized bound key handler + resolved key node
  Contexts -> Provider : InitializeContext(bound_key_handler, ...)
  Provider --> Contexts : initialized CSR handler
  Contexts --> Mediator : csr_context_id
  Mediator --> Client : csr_context_id
  Client --> App : ICsrGenerationContext\nkey and signature algorithm now fixed
end

group 4. Choose how to prepare generation input
alt [E] Eager setters
  App -> Client : csr.SetSubjectDn("CN=device.example,O=Example,C=DE")\noptional AddExtension(...) / AddSubjectAltName(...)
  loop Existing helper / validation requests as needed
  Client -> Mediator : CSR_PROCESS on csr_context_id\nDN/extension parsing and validation requests via SHM
  Mediator -> Provider : authenticate context ownership and forward\nto existing generation context handler
  Provider -> Executor : own context's Execute(input span, output span)
  Executor -> Executor : exact span contract and wire::Decode\nreject Generate and GenerateFromDer
  Executor -> Processor : own provider's Process(owned Document)
  Processor -> Native : existing native validation / codec bodies\nno bound-key access
  Native --> Processor : processed Document / native error
  Processor --> Executor : Document / mapped daemon error
  Executor -> Executor : same wire::Encode / capacity / response checks\nthen output copy
  Executor --> Provider : SHM document + one uint64 written-byte count
  Provider --> Mediator : processing result
  Mediator --> Client : processing response
  end
  Client -> Client : retain validated request data for Generate()
  Client --> App : subject/extensions accepted
else [B] ConfigureBatch: one validation IPC, no signing
  App -> Client : csr.ConfigureBatch(batch)
  Client -> Client : collect complete field descriptions locally\nno per-field helper requests
  Client -> Mediator : CSR_PROCESS on csr_context_id\nSCR1 ValidateBatch + all fields; SHM buffers
  Mediator -> Provider : authenticate ownership; forward to generation handler
  Provider -> Executor : own context's Execute(input span, output span)
  Executor -> Executor : validate spans / wire; reject both generation actions
  Executor -> Processor : Process(owned ValidateBatch Document)
  Processor -> Native : parse DN; validate complete batch\nno key access or signing
  Native --> Processor : complete normalized Document / error
  Processor --> Executor : Document / mapped error
  Executor -> Executor : on success: encode, check capacity\nallocate response before output copy
  Executor --> Provider : SCR1 + written count / error
  Provider --> Mediator : processing result
  Mediator --> Client : response
  alt Successful, complete and well-formed response
    Client -> Client : atomically replace complete snapshot\nclear eager SAN cache
    Client --> App : batch accepted; Generate() remains separate
  else Rejected batch or malformed response
    Client -> Client : preserve previous snapshot
    Client --> App : error; no partial commit
  end
else [D] Standalone DER input
  App -> App : prepare subject_dn_der and optional extensions_der\nno setters / ConfigureBatch / processing IPC
end
end

opt 5. Application explicitly requests signing using the already-bound key
alt [G] Current accepted eager / batch snapshot
  App -> Client : csr.Generate() (separate from ConfigureBatch)
  Client -> Mediator : CSR_GENERATE_NATIVE on csr_context_id\nneutral CSR input + output buffer via SHM\nno new key selection
else [D] One-operation DER generation
  App -> Client : csr.GenerateFromDer(subject_dn_der, extensions_der)
  Client -> Client : bounds checks and serialization only\nno DER parsing or builder mutation
  Client -> Mediator : SAME CSR_GENERATE_NATIVE on csr_context_id\nSCR1 GenerateFromDer=17 + DER fields; SHM buffers
end
  Mediator -> Provider : forward operation to that context's CSR handler
  Provider -> Provider : obtain already-bound key; create operation-local X509_REQ\nset version and bound public key
  alt [D] Strict standalone DER ingress
    Provider -[#B45309]> DerWire : D1: Decode(input); verify owned wire snapshot
    DerWire --[#B45309]> Provider : D1r: verified DER-only Document
    Provider -[#B45309]> DerInput : D2: validate both structures, then populate request
    DerInput --[#B45309]> Provider : D2r: populated fields
  else [G] Structured input
    Provider -> Provider : decode / revalidate complete snapshot\nencode extensions using bound SPKI; populate request
  end
  Provider -> Provider : after successful validation: sign with bound key\nverify signature; encode DER; check output capacity\nallocate response, then publish output bytes
  Provider --> Mediator : signed DER in output buffer + byte count
  Mediator --> Client : written-byte count
  Client -> Client : extract signed CSR bytes from output buffer
  Client --> App : ICsrExport
  App -> Client : GetEncodedCsrLength() / GetEncodedCsr(buffer)
  Client --> App : signed PKCS#10 DER bytes\nlocal export; no additional signing request
end

group 6. RELEASE context and caller-owned key reference
  App -> Client : destroy CSR context
  Client -> Mediator : CTX_CLOSE(csr_context_id)
  Mediator -> Keys : remove context subtree\nrelease its bound-key reference
  App -> Client : release/destroy key_guard
  Client -> Mediator : KEY_RELEASE(key_node_id)
  Mediator -> KeyExecutor : release caller-owned key reference
  KeyExecutor -> Keys : remove caller's key node\nunderlying key lifetime follows remaining references
  opt Standalone processing context was created
    App -> Client : destroy standalone processing context
    Client -> Mediator : CTX_CLOSE(processing_context_id)
    Mediator -> Processing : remove context node and destroy handler
  end
end

legend bottom
  Read top to bottom: connect -> optional helpers -> CREATE KEY -> BIND -> choose E / B / D -> SIGN -> RELEASE.
  Example: generated software EC key, then ECDSA-SHA256 CSR signing; no generic hardware signer is implied.
  The key reference selects the daemon-side private key during context creation only.
  PKCS#10 contains subject, public key, attributes/extensions and signature, not private-key bytes or the key reference.
  No certificate issuance, CA submission, persistent-key storage or new policy is introduced by this diagram.
  Eager: existing helper calls. Batch: one validation IPC plus separate Generate. DER: one generation IPC after setup.
endlegend
@enduml
